<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="ConfiguringOPCUAServerSecurityModes-A46415CC" xml:lang="en" class="- topic/topic task/task "><title class="- topic/title ">Configuring OPC UA Server Security Modes</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">Starting with <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/niagara4.14" class="- topic/keyword "> Niagara 4.14</keyword> to secure data, you need to configure the <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Security Mode</parmname> and the Server Security Certificate used
by the server to sign and encrypt communication messages. You must
select the Server Security Certificate from the <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/niagara" class="- topic/keyword "> Niagara 4.14</keyword> Key Store.</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">Configure</indexterm><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">Server
Security Modes</indexterm></keywords></metadata></prolog><taskbody class="- topic/body task/taskbody "><prereq class="- topic/section task/prereq "><ul class="- topic/ul "><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p ">A self-signed certificate, or a CA signed certificate in the <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">User Key Store</wintitle> is required for this procedure. For more
details refer the “Generating an OPC UA Server Certificate” .</p></li><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p "><keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/niagara4.14" class="- topic/keyword "> Niagara 4.14</keyword> or later version is required to support certificate-based
authorization.</p></li></ul></prereq><steps class="- topic/ol task/steps "><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">In the <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/Workbench" conref="../reuse/WH_SoftwareVariables_Tridium_N4_0000009934.dita#WHSoftwareVariablesTridium-9A3264AE/Workbench" class="- topic/keyword ">Workbench</keyword> Nav tree, expand <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Drivers</uicontrol></menucascade>, right-click the <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">OpcUaServer</uicontrol> and click <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Views</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Property Sheet</uicontrol></menucascade>.</cmd><stepresult class="- topic/itemgroup task/stepresult ">The <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Property Sheet</wintitle> opens.</stepresult></step><?Pub Caret -2?><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Expand <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Opc Tcp Endpoint</parmname> and click the appropriate check box to select the <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Security Mode</parmname> and <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Security Policies</parmname>.</cmd><info class="- topic/itemgroup task/info "><note class="- topic/note ">It is recommended to use the <userinput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/userinput ">SignEncrypt</userinput> mode and <userinput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/userinput ">Basic256Sha256</userinput> policy for high security.</note></info></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">In the <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">Cert Alias And Password</parmname> property,
click the drop-down <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Alias</uicontrol> to select the Server
Security Certificate and enter the private key <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Password</uicontrol>.</cmd></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">To save your changes, click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Save</uicontrol>.</cmd></step></steps></taskbody></task>